
# HG changeset patch
# User Welpy-cw <58345540+Welpy-cw@users.noreply.github.com>
# Date 1787674205 -3600
# Node ID 9c1603ae83211bedb9f25976359a6a655e187cb2
# Parent  3f83c2a25b8e2a6c1f4f9d5548fae9a8784bf95f
Bug 2065806 - Keep MSG_VIEW_FLAG_ISTHREAD on single-message thread roots. r=mkmelin

When deleting a message left a thread with only its root, the view
stripped MSG_VIEW_FLAG_ISTHREAD from the root row along with Elided and
MSG_VIEW_FLAG_HASCHILDREN. The twisty correctly disappeared, but
ISTHREAD is not just a UI hint: ReverseThreads() uses it to find thread
boundaries when reversing the sort order. With the flag gone, a later
sort-order toggle dropped the root row from m_keys/m_flags/m_levels,
making the message vanish from the list until the folder was re-entered
or compacted.

Keep ISTHREAD and clear only Elided | HASCHILDREN - that is sufficient
to flatten the row in the UI (expand/collapse already requires both
HASCHILDREN and ISTHREAD). Fixed in two places:
- nsMsgDBView::OnHdrDeleted() (message deleted while hidden in a
  collapsed thread)
- nsMsgThreadedDBView::RemoveByIndex() (visible message deleted)

The same pattern exists in nsMsgSearchDBView::RemoveByIndex() but was
left alone: cross-folder threads couldn't be made to exhibit the bug.

Based on research by alta88.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320680


